Syntax of predicate logic : We have constants a,b,c
			Unary and binary predicate symbols P,Q,R
			Variables x,y,z

A predicate horn clause is a disjunction of literals with exactly one positive literal

Semantics of predicate logic : 
Unary predicates are used to define the property of an object
Binary predicates show relationships between two objects

Intepretation based semantics : 

An interpretation has a domain and an Intepretation function
