Correctness :
We must guarantee this method is Complete and Sound. 
Completeness is shown since every consequence is found
Soundness if followed since every fact is true for all models

Completeness : 
If the canonical interpretation does not satisfy P(a) then it is not entailed in the KB
If it is entailed then it should appear in the canonical model

Soundness : 
If the canonical model states P(a) to be true then it should be true for all models

